TITAN migration policy (Vol 3 §13.2)
====================================

Migrations are HAND-WRITTEN. There is no autogenerate-and-commit workflow:

1. Write each revision by hand under versions/, stating in the docstring which
   spec section (Vol 3 §6) the schema change implements.
2. `alembic revision` (without --autogenerate) may scaffold the file; the
   upgrade()/downgrade() bodies are authored and reviewed by a human or agent
   reading the spec — never generated by diffing models.
3. Every revision must have a working downgrade().
4. One revision per phase-sized change; never edit a merged revision — add a
   new one.
5. Run with `make migrate` (alembic upgrade head); the database URL comes from
   TITAN_DATABASE_URL via titan.settings.
